# PassReady — Cursor / agent rules

## Tech stack
- Frontend: Next.js (App Router, TypeScript)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS
- Backend: Next.js API routes
- Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL)
- Auth: Supabase Auth (later)
- Payments: Stripe
- AI: OpenAI API

## Code
- TypeScript everywhere; functional React components
- Modular, reusable files; clean architecture without over-layering

## API
- REST handlers; validate all inputs with Zod
- Never trust client-submitted data for security or billing decisions

## Security
- No API keys in client bundles; env vars for secrets
- Sanitize inputs; rate-limit public/sensitive API routes
- Protect PII; GDPR-minded collection and retention

## Performance
- Prefer server-side logic; avoid unnecessary re-renders
- Target fast API responses; design for concurrency (stateless routes)

## Product (MVP)
- Flow: homepage → assessment form → pay £4.99 → AI report
- Outputs: pass probability, top risks, personalised improvement plan
- AI tone: professional instructor — specific, actionable, not generic

## Build approach
- MVP first; simple and fast; validate with users; iterate from feedback
